  (text "SOUND CHIP: the YM2612 and the level shifters that let the 3.3V Pico talk to the 5V chip\nData bus: 74LVC245A at 3.3V. GP11 (/RD) sets its direction: high = Pico writes to the chip, low = Pico reads the\nbusy flag. The firmware must switch GP0-GP7 to inputs before pulling /RD low.\nControl lines: 74HCT541 at 5V. 100 ohm series resistors on every chip pin protect the YM2612.\n/CS is tied low, so the chip listens whenever /WR or /RD is pulsed. /IRQ is not used.\nClock: full-size or half-size oscillator can at 7.670454 MHz (NTSC Genesis), 33 ohm series resistor.\nPut the YM2612 in a socket. Keep the clock wire short and away from the audio wiring." (at 25.4 22.86 0)
    (effects (font (size 1.5 1.5)) (justify left top))
    (uuid 24790787-087a-56f1-9776-fa088a81d407)
  )
  (text "One 100nF capacitor right at each chip's power pin:\nU2, U3, X1, U5, U4 = YM2612 (plus 47uF at the YM2612)" (at 266.7 193.04 0)
    (effects (font (size 1.5 1.5)) (justify left top))
    (uuid e3289f94-81a3-5b7a-9448-0e17edb184ac)
  )
)
